    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4275",
      "problem": "Consider the diagram shown above. If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/ff8e895a778e6dd6c5a0af96719cd06aca1b52de0dd7705a6aa95b893b5f1613.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/cf191e748f291f3c41ff3b4627f9ea67f438c0fc9eab304147497b0184996d70.svg), Find the exact value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/7ac5f7f77af01ba3bab7ec2d9829d3744a1545174ffc9f1746a5216dd8a5ac4c.svg) \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/922fa6572855e2a40f2b0fdd97bbbc5d6ddf2323228d99d5ab74a7aa7c2072f8.png)",
      "worked_solution": "We can interpret the subtraction \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/25262e79200c8e994f31332acd934162d54d0f98b0195a6eec3932c16b9622af.svg)\nas the addition\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/354fa7ad258940b74d98a0453c2d11b86938d5c21972bb2cfb49034da76e88f6.svg)\n\nThe vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/6c5c8d4958cf6c35565ac5bcf1f3fae2ac63ae79a4322663137c8c9911bd9a1b.svg) has the same magnitude as ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/639196a1a30d6f6280e3cf491e6cf3c2b0b991892970f7b641a9b300defb034f.svg) and the direction that is opposite to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/eca1ed153026ae1dd1f864e88a95c50f535fe5c5ee0395081ef337c7d4fcb478.svg) We use the triangle law of addition to find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/527e0abeb684dd24d8c92e45425542080c4c9493b9460bb89753fef3226c1f92.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/32817decbc6ba29aecc19b148b0d390c3965f4b3095952e41d02bc885b6275a7.svg) The resultant goes from the start of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/527e0abeb684dd24d8c92e45425542080c4c9493b9460bb89753fef3226c1f92.svg) to the head of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/b80fb98a5bce5dbfd122ab9a6905b521ac129b69acd38f81f8674415b26602d3.svg) as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/5012173859939fe084fa20f01d3d1f3a07d00bd2e9e2f0432743a7e2e4e1cd19.png)\n\nSo, we can use the law of cosines as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/4e25b73e214697d6173adf6c833ab41376fa2b98ed4df62f57f6f1c5109a27be.svg)\n\nHence, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/c855843d6fff0751c076c876ec0cfa2583f9ccc19e9b793bf6ade5e2356b4087.svg)",
